Hi Sean,

Following your 13 May review, FCR-REV-2025-001, I've revised the four questio=
ns and attached the learner replacement sheet David approved yesterday. Each =
now asks for the feasibility of both routes, the supporting condition and the=
 next action separately.

- Q04 compares 18 and 22 kits with two staff available and an 11:40 Wednesday=
 receipt time.
- Q08 keeps 18 kits and the same receipt time, but compares one available sta=
ff member with two.
- Q11 keeps the quantity at 22 and compares receipt at 11:40 and 12:10. At th=
e later time neither route is available under the stated conditions.
- Q15 starts with 18 kits and staff availability unconfirmed. Learners must i=
dentify what to check and what to do before the noon deadline without treatin=
g an unconfirmed number as a confirmed shortage.

The sheet replaces those four numbered questions; the other twelve and the or=
der remain in place. We'll use it with the booklet on 28 May.

Thank you for showing us where a single fact was enough to answer the old que=
stions.

Best,
Heather


